      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Preview Image clamps to [0,1], so the result will look blown out -- that is the preview, not the data. Wire `images` into an EXR writer (e.g. BAT Video Combine, format image/exr-sequence) to keep the real scene-linear values.\n\nThe small preview under Encode shows the mask the model will reconstruct. Tune over_threshold until it covers the clipped areas and nothing else, or connect your own MASK to Encode.\n\nPick your own files in the Load Model node -- the names here are placeholders.\n\nEquirectangular HDRI: note Encode mode=panorama and the DiffHDR_Pano LoRA on the loader -- both are required, they go together. A batch of panoramas is processed one at a time."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
